# Dashboards

The allocation surface (`AllocationBoard`, classes prefixed `da-` in `apps/web/styles/globals.css`) is the baseline. A dashboard reuses those classes. It does not invent a second header, KPI strip, table, or status pill.

Wrap the view in `da`.

## Page

1. `da-crumbs` — trail, slash separators, current name in `strong`.
2. `da-ribbon` — one identity band:
   - `da-title`: `da-chip` for the stage, serif `h1`, one sentence, optional `da-track` for a sequence.
   - `da-facts`: labeled facts. One `da-fact big` holds the headline number. The label is muted; the value is weight 500.
   - `da-holdbox`: the single decision or coverage for the page. Serif number, one sentence, `da-bar`.
3. `da-tabs` — sections of this workspace. The active tab is `on` (3px teal underline). A section that is not built yet stays visible and `disabled`.
4. Each block is `da-sec` with `da-sechead`: title on the left, a helper sentence or `page-actions` on the right.

## Work surface

- Peer objects are `da-cards` / `da-card`. Color is a 3px top edge. One serif figure per card (`da-size`).
- A composition is `da-stack` of `da-seg`, with `da-axis` labeling the ends.
- A working table is `da-grid` inside `da-gridwrap`. A cell is a value plus a muted `small`. Numbers are right-aligned (`num`). The selected row is `sel`.
- The selection’s detail is `da-panel` beside the grid (`da-main`). Lead with `da-big`, then `da-mini` or a plain table, then `da-rule` rows.
- Status is `da-st`: `ok`, `near`, `bind`, `breach`, `na`. A gauge is `da-gauge` with the same suffix.
- Actions use `btn`. One `btn btn-primary` completes the screen.
- The main surface shows the name a person uses: the deal, the fund, the rule, the attribute. It does not show the attribute code, the rule code, or the entity code. Those identifiers stay on the detail screen.

```tsx
<div className="da">
  <header className="da-ribbon">
    <div className="da-title">
      <span className="da-chip">Diligence</span>
      <h1>Project Brightwater</h1>
      <p>Add-on ready unitranche with revolver.</p>
    </div>
    <div className="da-facts">
      <div className="da-fact big"><span>Total facility</span><strong>$250.0M</strong></div>
    </div>
    <div className="da-holdbox">
      <div className="da-holdtop"><span>Our hold</span><b>50%</b></div>
      <div className="da-bar"><i style={{ width: '50%' }} /></div>
    </div>
  </header>
</div>
```

## Leave these out

- `page-header` and `page-title` are for admin lists, not dashboards.
- `AppGrid` is for registers. A deal, fund, pipeline, or compliance workspace uses `da-grid`.
- Do not add a new class prefix for a dashboard. Extend `da-` only when the existing classes cannot express the layout.
